# Domain Zero Protocol - per-install privacy (distro template)
# Shipped as the published repo's .gitignore so fresh installs keep local data local.
.protocol-state/trigger-19.md
.protocol-state/authorization/session-state.json
.protocol-state/authorization/authorization.log
.protocol-state/custom-agent-registry.json
.protocol-state/security/*.lock
.protocol-state/research/**/*.raw.log
.protocol-state/backups/
*.backup
*.backup.*
.dzp-killswitch/
.protocol-state/brain/brain.db
.protocol-state/brain/cortex-snapshot.md
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# SEC-BRAIN-007: additional brain-directory backstop entries (2026-06-14)
.protocol-state/brain/memories/
.protocol-state/brain/model-cache/
.protocol-state/brain/index.log
.protocol-state/brain/index.lock

# v9.2.0 Script Orchestration — the "DEV-ONLY" ignore block that used to live here
# (dzp.py / script_coordinator.py / script_dependencies.yaml) was REVERSED by USER
# ruling 2026-07-19: this orchestration trio now SHIPS (fulfills ISS-084/ISS-085,
# which already added it to publish-manifest.yaml's include_files/include_state and
# to manifest_completeness_offenders() Scope 5 in dzp_publish_core.py). This
# distro.gitignore block was the actual root cause of BUG-DISTRO-ORCH-TRIO-001: it
# silently caused every published DZP-vX.Y.Z branch's `git add -A` (run against the
# distro/.gitignore this file becomes) to SKIP the three files even though the
# manifest correctly staged them to disk and both completeness gates reported green
# (they only ever checked manifest TEXT / the staged FILESYSTEM, never actual git
# tracking) — see scripts/distro/dzp_publish_core.py::manifest_tracking_offenders()
# for the new fail-closed gate that closes this blind spot going forward.

# FEAT-IDGOV-001 (v9.10.0, Phase G4/G5): per-wrapper signing secrets and the
# registry lockfile are LOCAL, per-install runtime artifacts, never committed
# by a consumer install either. The real issue-registry.jsonl itself is NOT
# ignored here -- once a consumer activates issue governance it becomes their
# own append-only committed audit ledger, same as the two protected records.
.protocol-state/.idgov-tokens/
*.jsonl.lock

# BUG-CORTEX-008 R5 (v9.10.0, Megumi Tier-3 P2-2): detached Cortex step
# output (script_coordinator.py `detach: true` mode) writes a rolling
# diagnostic log here; local runtime artifact, never committed.
.protocol-state/logs/

# N1-C (v9.11.0): repo-root backups/. The agent backup procedure historically mandated
# ./backups/[timestamp]/, which was never ignored here -- a consumer following it produced an
# untracked-but-committable tree of verbatim copies. The mandate now points at
# .protocol-state/backups/ (protocol/yuuji.agent.md); this entry protects installs that already
# created the old directory under the previous instructions.
/backups/
